From 9fb0c27126327601e4bbf26a37c6e8837e1bef49 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: terminills <tdeters@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 8 Aug 2026 11:38:17 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 549/638] AROS: guard worker startup during shutdown

Add an AROS process-wide child shutdown flag so off-thread service worker startup checks do not dereference ChildProcess::current() during teardown. Suppress late dedicated/service worker startup once renderer shutdown has begun.

Make AROS service-worker ping timeouts observe-only and single-shot. YouTube playback can keep the renderer visibly alive while the service worker Mojo ping does not reach the worker context thread, so do not stop the worker from the watchdog; retain AROS ping/stage telemetry for the hosted replay.

Evidence: build173 chrome sha256 fa90761fc45261927e5b205be2a36815284dc288534b06330bc6887364ea0009 copied into hosted with matching hash. run106 reached YouTube, started sw.js, sent one ping, logged one timeout observe-only, did not emit 'Service Worker is not responding', and did not repeat the timeout in the sampled window.
